SUMMARY:Radu Paponiu Conducts Concerto Competition Winners with the SFCM O
 rchestra
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261003T193000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261003T210000
DTSTAMP:20261006T001646Z
UID:funcheap-1638704@sf-cal
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:Live Music Event
DESCRIPTION:Submitted by the Event OrganizerSan Francisco Symphony Youth O
 rchestra Music Director Radu Paponiu guides three SFCM student competition
  winners through the concertos of their choice.\nGuitarist Kaz Hudson will
  be playing Mario Castelnuovo-Tedesco’s Guitar Concerto No. 1 in D Major
 \, Op. 99\; violinist Mark Chen Sergei Prokofiev’s Violin Concerto No. 1
  in D Major\, Op. 19\; and cellist Lekai Li closes the evening with Willia
 m Walton’s Cello Concerto.\n\nSFCM’s annual Concerto Competition offer
 s the student body the opportunity to star with the Conservatory Orchestra
 . This includes public orchestral workshops with distinguished guest condu
 ctors\, like Donald Runnicles\, Carl St. Clair\, Nicola Luisotti\, and Pet
 er Oundjian.\nPrior to his current role\, Radu served as Associate Conduct
 or of the Naples Philharmonic for five years\, and seven as Music Director
  of the Philharmonic’s Youth Orchestra. He also served as Music Director
  for the Southwest Florida Symphony Orchestra\, and has guested with symph
 ony orchestras in San Francisco\, Dallas\, St. Louis\, Rhode Island\, Loui
 siana\, Illinois\, Colorado\, and North Carolina. Aside from Naples\, his 
 international performances have included Berlin\, Romania\, Bologna\, and 
 Transylvania.\nPresented by San Francisco Conservatory of Music\n\nFree\n\
 nTickets: https://sfcm.edu/\nDetails: https://sf.funcheap.com/radu-paponiu
 -conducts-concerto-competition-winners-sfcm-orchestra/\nSource: Funcheap S
 F
