DESCRIPTION:Submitted by the Event OrganizerLisa Mezzacappa 5(ish)\, with 
 special guest The Holly MartinsLisa Mezzacappa 5(ish)\nAaron Bennett – t
 enor sax\nMark Clifford – vibraphone\nBrett Carson – piano\nJordan Gle
 nn – drums\nLisa Mezzacappa – bass\nBerkeley bassist and composer Lisa
  Mezzacappa brings the latest incarnation of her working band to The Back 
 Room for a raucous and rollicking suite of original music.\n\nHer 5(ish) e
 nsemble plays selections from its 2026 release othrwrldly\, which explores
  the concept of worldbuilding—inspired by Mezzacappa’s fascination wit
 h the speculative fiction of Ursula Le Guin\, Haruki Murakami\, Samuel R. 
 Delany and David Mitchell— as a way to envision new kinds of musical int
 eraction\, storytelling\, structure and play.\nothrwrldly showcases her ba
 nd’s spectacular chemistry and keen improvisational prowess\, woven into
  expansive compositions that foreground energy\, sound\, interaction and s
 urprise. The band includes longtime collaborators tenor saxophonist Aaron 
 Bennett (Adam Lane’s Full Throttle Orchestra)\, vibraphonist Mark Cliffo
 rd (Meerna\, Rent Romus)\, and drummer Jordan Glenn (Fred Frith Trio\, Zee
 na Parkins)\, plus recent addition pianist Brett Carson (Art Ensemble of C
 hicago\, Roscoe Mitchell).\n\nThe Holly Martins\nLorin Benedict\, voice\nK
 asey Knidsen\, alto saxophone\nEric Vogler\, guitar\nNamed after the main 
 character in the classic postwar film\, The Third Man\, The Holly Martins 
 is a trio of Bay Area musicians dedicated to exploring the boundaries of j
 azz-infused i...\n\n$20.00\n\nTickets: https://eventvesta.com/events/16068
 4/t/tickets\nDetails: https://sf.funcheap.com/lisa-mezzacappa-5ish-raucous
 -original-jazz-berkeley/\nSource: Funcheap SF
IMAGE;VALUE=URI:https://cdn.funcheap.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/09/unname
 d-1.jpg
LAST-MODIFIED:20261006T001646Z
LOCATION:The Back Room\, 1984 Bonita Ave Berkeley\, CA 94704
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
URL:https://sf.funcheap.com/lisa-mezzacappa-5ish-raucous-original-jazz-ber
 keley/
