 AM to 4 PM\, Off the Grid returns to Treasure Island\, bringing food truck
 s\, music\, and family-friendly activities to Cityside Park in San Francis
 co’s newest waterfront neighborhood.\nThe spring series includes free ki
 te flying\, face painting\, and plenty of open space to relax\, making it 
 an easy outing for all ages. Admission is free\, and complimentary ferry s
 ervice from the San Francisco Ferry Building is available with RSVP.\nWhat
  to Expect:\n\nOne Island. 15+ Creators. Multiple Cuisines.\nMore than 15 
 food creators per event span Vietnamese\, Korean\, Japanese\, Hawaiian\, M
 exican\, Italian\, German\, BBQ\, fried chicken\, sandwiches\, and sweets.
  There’s something for every craving\, from go-to favorites to something
  entirely new.\nA Waterfront Setting with Unbeatable Views\nCityside Park 
 spans six acres along the shoreline\, with open lawns\, wide promenades\, 
 and views that stretch from the Bay Bridge to the Golden Gate. Settle in\,
  explore the park\, and take in the full sweep of the Bay.\nKites Over the
  Bay\nThe signature kite program returns\, with complimentary kites availa
 ble with signup. By midday\, the sky fills with color\, creating one of th
 e most shareable scenes of the season.\nAn Island Adventure Eight Minutes 
 from the Ferry Building\nLeave the city and arrive somewhere that feels no
 thing like it. Just eight minutes by ferry from downtown San Francisco\, O
 ff...\n\nFree\n\nTickets: http://www.offthegrid.com/treasureisland\nDetail
 s: https://sf.funcheap.com/off-the-grid-2026-treasure-island-w-free-kites-
 free-ferry-rides-fall-2026-4/\nSource: Funcheap SF
