DESCRIPTION:Submitted by the Event OrganizerJenette SellinAfter a long sum
 mer hiatus\, Balkan Sundays is back! We’ll be at Muddy Waters on 2nd Sun
 days and Ashkenaz on 4th Sundays (starting in October). This coming Balkan
  Sundays on October 11th will feature Duygu and Friends with a Turkish mus
 ic jam session that the band will lead.\nCome one come all to play some of
  your favorite Turkish repertoire. The first half of the evening will feat
 ure Duygu and Friends\, then the 2nd half will be opened up as a jam sessi
 on. As always\, it’s free. All we ask is that you support the venue by b
 uying some of their delicious food and beverages and it’s always suggest
 ed to tip the band. That’s how we keep cover free events happening. See 
 you there!\n\nDuygu & Friends covers folk songs from Anatolia and the broa
 der Mediterranean\, spanning multiple languages and musical traditions. Jo
 ining Duygu Gün on guitar and vocals are Peter Bonos on oud and trumpet\,
  Evin Sellin on violin\, Zina Pozen on accordion\, and Aaron Goldstein on 
 percussion.\nFind them on IG: duybeni\n\nFree\n\nTickets: https://www.inst
 agram.com/balkansundays/\nDetails: https://sf.funcheap.com/balkan-sundays-
 duygu-friends-turkish-music-jam-session/\nSource: Funcheap SF
